<%#
  Printable faction card sheets. Self-contained like the other public pages (privacy,
  account-deletion): no application layout, no login. The rows come straight from the files
  FactionCardPdf wrote into public/cards/pdf.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="robots" content="all">
  <title>Printable Cards — Carnevale Companion</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: #1a1a1a;
      background: #f7f7f8;
    }
    .wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.25rem 5rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 2.25rem 0 .5rem; }
    .meta { color: #666; font-size: .9rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    a { color: #2f6f4f; }
    ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    li { margin: .3rem 0; }
    footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1); color: #666; font-size: .875rem; }

    .sheets { list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
    .sheets li { margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
    .sheet {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .9rem;
      padding: .85rem 1.1rem;
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1);
      border-radius: 12px;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
    }
    .sheet:hover { border-color: #2f6f4f; }
    .sheet .name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; }
    .sheet .detail { color: #666; font-size: .85rem; }
    .sheet .grow { flex: 1; }
    .sheet .action { color: #2f6f4f; font-weight: 600; font-size: .9rem; white-space: nowrap; }
    .swatch { width: 10px; height: 34px; border-radius: 3px; flex: none; }
    .empty { padding: 1.1rem; background: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1); border-radius: 12px; color: #666; }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      body { color: #e6e6e6; background: #17181a; }
      .meta, footer, .sheet .detail, .empty { color: #9aa0a6; }
      a { color: #6fbf95; }
      footer { border-top-color: rgba(255,255,255,.12); }
      .sheet, .empty { background: #202124; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,.12); }
      .sheet:hover { border-color: #6fbf95; }
      .sheet .action { color: #6fbf95; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 480px) {
      .sheet { flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .sheet .grow { flex-basis: 100%; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="wrap">
    <h1>Printable Cards</h1>
    <p class="meta">Carnevale Companion &middot; one PDF per faction, ready to print and cut</p>

    <p>
      Every model in a faction, as a print-ready PDF. Each page holds one card &mdash; its front and
      back side by side &mdash; at the exact tarot size of <strong>70 &times; 120&nbsp;mm</strong>, with
      thin crop marks to cut against. Cards run in the same order as the app: Leaders first, then
      Heroes, then Henchmen, alphabetical within each.
    </p>

    <% if @sheets.any? %>
      <ul class="sheets">
        <% @sheets.each do |sheet| %>
          <li>
            <a class="sheet" href="<%= sheet.url %>" download>
              <span class="swatch" style="<%= faction_swatch_style(sheet.faction) %>"></span>
              <span>
                <span class="name"><%= sheet.faction.capitalize %></span><br>
                <span class="detail">
                  Cards as of <%= sheet.date.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>
                  &middot; <%= number_to_human_size(sheet.byte_size) %>
                </span>
              </span>
              <span class="grow"></span>
              <span class="action">Download PDF &darr;</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% else %>
      <p class="empty">
        The print sheets have not been generated yet. Please check back shortly.
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <h2>Printing them</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Print at <strong>100% / actual size</strong>. Any &ldquo;fit to page&rdquo; or
        &ldquo;shrink oversized pages&rdquo; option will scale the cards off tarot size &mdash; turn it off.</li>
      <li>Use A4 paper. Card stock of around 250&ndash;300&nbsp;g/m&sup2; holds up far better in play than
        ordinary paper.</li>
      <li>Cut along the crop marks: the four short lines around each card meet at its corners.</li>
      <li>The front and back of a card sit next to each other on the same page, so nothing needs to be
        printed double-sided &mdash; cut both out and glue or sleeve them back to back.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Keeping up to date</h2>
    <p>
      The date in each file name is the day those cards were generated. Corrections happen, so if you
      printed a card a while ago it is worth comparing against the current sheet &mdash; or against the
      card in the app, which always shows the latest version.
    </p>

    <footer>
      Carnevale is a trademark of its respective owner. This companion app is an unofficial,
      fan-made tool and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the publisher of the game.
      See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </footer>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
